<<
/Author (Hunter Hughes)
/CreationDate (D\07220261111141453\05505\04700\047)
/Creator (H Heuristics PDF pipeline)
/Keywords (sustainable convergence\054 economic convergence\054 sustainable development\054 polycrisis resilience\054 Global South\054 emerging economies\054 technology diffusion\054 clean energy transition\054 decoupling\054 development economics\054 Sustainable Convergence Index\054 scenarios to 2100)
/ModDate (D\07220261111141453\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (Billions of people still live with large gaps in income\054 health\054 technology and public services\056 Closing those gaps is the central task of this century\054 and doing it without wrecking the climate\054 the air and the systems everyone depends on is the second\056 This report argues that the two must be answered together and gives the combined answer a name\072 Sustainable Convergence\054 a concept developed by Hunter Hughes\054 Founder of H Heuristics\056 It defines Sustainable Convergence as the process through which emerging and developing economies progressively narrow economic\054 technological\054 institutional and human\055development gaps with advanced economies while pursuing environmentally sustainable\054 socially inclusive and systemically resilient development pathways\054 and it relates the concept to the companion concept of Polycrisis Resilience\056)
/Title (Sustainable Convergence\072 Sustainable Development and Global Economic Convergence\072 How Emerging Economies Can Close the Gaps Without Repeating the Mistakes of the Past)
/Trapped /False
>>
endobj
